fix(domain): on a runner, route calls from background fibers through the cluster

Against alchemy `packages/domain/src` at 33c10dd (2.0.0-beta.87). Apply from the
repository root with `git apply`; the text above the first `---` line is ignored.

## Problem

On a runner, `DomainCluster.layerEntities` builds the platform's namespace as
`makeNamespace(objects, { url: "", token: "", service: "" })`.
`makeNamespace(...).getByName` (in `@alchemy.run/effect-cluster`) routes a call
through Effect Cluster only when `Sharding` is in the calling fiber's context;
otherwise it uses the gateway's HTTP client, here with an empty URL.

Entity handlers run with `Sharding`. Fibers that the model's Layer starts while
it builds do not: the runner bootstrap builds the entrypoint Layer before the
cluster Layer exists. So any call from such a fiber fails with
`RpcClientError: HttpError: InvalidUrl (POST /rpc/)`. This covers a stream's
`list`, a view's `get` and a command's `send` alike; it is not specific to
reads.

Seen with a consumer that polls another context's fact stream from a Layer
(`Effect.forkScoped`) on the runners: every read failed, the fact was
published and never consumed, and a run waiting for an approval never
concluded.

## Change

In runner mode only:

- the Layer the runner launches inside the cluster (`runner.value.host(hosted,
  ...)`, where the workflow engine is already captured) also captures the
  runner's `Sharding` in a `Deferred`;
- the namespace passed to `remote` gives a call whose fiber has no `Sharding`
  that one, waiting until the runner has joined. A call that already has
  `Sharding` goes through unchanged.

## Why it is safe

- Calls from entity handlers are unchanged (they have `Sharding`).
- A background call made before the runner has joined now waits for it
  instead of failing, as workflow calls already wait for `started`.
- No wire protocol change; one file. Callers (caller mode, through the
  gateway) are untouched.

An alternative is to make `makeNamespace` itself fall back to a runner-wide
`Sharding` in `@alchemy.run/effect-cluster`; this change keeps the fix inside
`@alchemy.run/domain`, where the empty URL is chosen.

## Tests

On Effect Cluster with Postgres (two runners on a local swarm): a runs inbox
polling Party's fact stream on the runners consumed the decision; a run
waiting for approval completed after approval across a runner restart, and
across a `pg_dump` and restore into a fresh stack. There is no in-memory test:
reproducing it needs the runner bootstrap.

